## Concurrency model

- **Per-key locks** (`src/keyed-lock.js`). Each store key has its own FIFO
  queue. `reserve`, `commit`, `release` and `expire` lock the order key, then
  the order's SKU keys. `addStock` locks its SKU key. A call waits only for
  calls that lock one of the same keys, so calls that share no SKU and no
  order run in parallel. There is no service-wide lock (see INC-5490).
- **Bundles can queue a second SKU behind a busy one.** A bundle holds the
  SKUs it has already locked while it waits for the rest. If `laces` sorts
  before `sneaker-limited`, a `[laces, sneaker-limited]` bundle holds `laces`
  while it queues behind the sneaker traffic, and a laces-only order waits
  behind that bundle. Avoiding this would mean letting later calls overtake a
  waiting bundle, and a bundle containing the hot SKU could then starve.
- **Lock order.** At most one order key is held at a time, and it is always
  taken before any SKU key. SKU keys are taken in sorted order. Because every
